CoreML's decoder models (i.e., models created using the Create ML Decoders feature) use a technique called constant reuse of "k-value cache" to speed up inference. This technique stores the output of a particular layer in the model for the same input values across multiple evaluations. This way, instead of recalculating the same output every time, the model can quickly fetch the pre-calculated output from the cache, saving computational resources. This is particularly useful for models that involve recurrent neural networks or convolutional neural networks as they can have many layers where the same inputs are used multiple times.
