When you train or predict on a large dataset, it might not fit into memory entirely. By using streaming, your model processes input in chunks instead, and a streaming callback lets you handle intermediate results as they come, allowing for more efficient memory usage and providing flexible ways to monitor or customize the model's output during processing.

